ub.com/users/om7057/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I pulled this into a worktree and ran the full suite (`go vet ./...`, `go build ./...`, `go test ./...` across the whole `tool` module). Everything passes clean.\n\nTo check the fix actually does something, I reverted `match.go` and `filter.go` back to `main` while keeping this PR's new test files (`match_test.go`, `find_test.go`), which still compiled since the `Dependency.IsTest` plumbing lives in `find.go`. With `main`'s matching logic, the new tests fail exactly where you'd expect. `TestRunMatch_FileRuleWhere/is_test_true_skips_a_normal_build`, `is_test_false_skips_the_generated_test_main`, both `has_func` cases, `TestRunMatch_FileRuleWhereBuildError`, `TestPreciseMatching_IsTestFromDependency`, and two of the `TestRunMatch_FileRuleWherePackageLevel` cases all fail with \"Should be empty, but was [add_to_main]\". That's the file rule firing when `where` should have excluded it, the exact bug from #1347. Restoring the two files makes them all pass again.\n\nI also tried reproducing the CLI-level repro from #1347 in a scratch workspace, two modules, `otelc go build` vs `otelc go test`, but hit module-wiring issues getting my scratch `myrules` module recognized as a dependency at all. That's on my repro setup, not the PR. The unit tests already isolate the exact bug from the issue so I didn't chase it further.\n\nTwo things I'd flag:\n- `TestRunMatch_FileRuleWhereBuildError` looks like it checks that a malformed `where` on a file rule now errors at load time. Worth confirming that's what actually ships, since the PR description says both the error-at-load-time and evaluate-it-properly paths landed.\n- The package-level `has_struct`/`not`/`all-of` semantics (checking against the union of all files in the package, not per-file) is a real behavior choice, not just a bug fix. `not: {has_func: X}` ends up stricter than a per-file reading would suggest, worth calling that out explicitly since it's not obvious from the issue.\n\nTest coverage looks good, and `docs/rules.md` got a short note.\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/1360#pullrequestreview-5254929137","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/1360","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/1360#pullrequestreview-5254929137"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/1360"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-19T06:56:06Z","commit_id":"8f6bbee5337dce3291c7ba9176ae12077320f5b2"},{"id":5278238852,"node_id":"PRR_kwDONpzSS88AAAABOpuIhA","user":{"login":"amazingakai","id":93782497,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZcB4Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93782497?u=636eb3c0c0e15f40e91bd088e19b41718b12ddeb&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai","html_url":"https://github.com/amazingakai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amazingakai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url